# {{NAME}} (Grayjay plugin)

TypeScript Grayjay plugin, built with the grayjay devkit (`gj`).

## Commands

| Command | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `bun run test` | build + run tests under `bun:test` (offline, mocked http) |
| `bun run build` | emit `dist/{{SAFE_NAME}}Config.json` + `{{SAFE_NAME}}Script.js` |
| `bun run release` | build signed + minified + version bump |
| `bun run serve` | serve `dist/` on the LAN (QR code) for the Grayjay DevServer |
| `bun run validate` | validate config, bundle and signature |

## Releasing (stable URL)

Push a tag or merge to master: `.github/workflows/release.yml` builds and
uploads the plugin to a **fixed `release` tag**. Its asset URLs never change:

```
https://github.com/YOU/REPO/releases/download/release/{{SAFE_NAME}}Config.json
```

Set `sourceUrl` in `grayjay.config.ts` to that URL once — the app will poll it
for updates. Add your signing key as the `GRAYJAY_SIGNING_KEY` repository
secret (base64 of the PEM created by `gj build --sign`) so releases stay
signed by the same author.

## Layout

- `grayjay.config.ts` — plugin manifest (typed via `defineConfig`)
- `src/index.ts` — plugin code, typed by ambient engine globals
- `src/index.test.ts` — contract tests (`@grayjay/tester`)
